      "description": "",
      "bio": "Dr Santosh Kumar Yadav (Ayurveda Doctor) BAMS, PGDAyDS, Dip Yoga, CCYP, ATMS, AAA Founder – Ayurveda Yoga Wellness Clinic, Melbourne Clinical Director & Principal Ayurvedic Practitioner | Integrative Health Consultant Dr Santosh Kumar Yadav is the Founder, Clinical Director, and Principal Ayurveda Doctor at Ayurveda Yoga Wellness Clinic, Melbourne. A highly respected Ayurvedic Practitioner with over 20 years of clinical experience in Australia & India, Dr Santosh has dedicated his life to the science of Ayurveda and holistic wellness. He holds a Bachelor of Ayurvedic Medicine and Surgery (BAMS) from the University of Lucknow and a Postgraduate Diploma in Ayurvedic Drug Standardization (PGDAyDS) from the internationally renowned Banaras Hindu University (BHU), India. Additionally, he is certified in Yoga with a Diploma in Yoga and Certificate in Yoga Practice (CCYP). Dr Santosh is a Registered Accredited Practitioner with the Australian Traditional Medicine Society (ATMS) and a Professional Member of the Australasian Association of Ayurveda Inc. (AAA) and a Member with Yoga Australia Inc. as a Yoga Teacher. Over the years, he has worked in a wide range of clinical settings across India and Australia, successfully treating thousands of patients, with a focus on chronic disease management, detoxification, and Panchakarma therapies. Dr. Santosh is passionate about bridging traditional Ayurveda with modern healthcare, creating a calm and nurturing space where healing unfolds naturally. His integrative and heart-centered approach supports each individual on their journey toward optimal wellness—physically, mentally, and emotionally. Holistic & Individualized Ayurvedic Consultations & Treatment Approaches Dr Santosh’s approach is rooted in classical Ayurvedic principles, enhanced with modern diagnostic insights. During a consultation, he provides a thorough assessment that includes: Dosha & Constitution Analysis (Prakriti/Vikriti) Pulse & Tongue Diagnosis Holistic Ayurvedic Consultation Diet & Lifestyle Recommendations Panchakarma Detox & Rejuvenation Therapies Herbal Medicine & Rasayana Support Emotional Wellbeing & Ayurvedic Counselling Preventive & Seasonal Health Guidance Integration with Modern Medical Insights Based on this integrated analysis, he formulates a personalized treatment plan using Ayurvedic medicines, diet, lifestyle guidance, and therapeutic procedures. Dr Yadav Specialized Ayurvedic Treatments At Ayurveda Yoga Wellness Clinic, we offer authentic Ayurvedic care for a wide range of health conditions: Musculoskeletal & Joint Disorders Arthritis (Osteoarthritis, Rheumatoid Arthritis, Gout) Chronic joint pain Back and Neck Pain Fertility & Women’s Health Male and Female Infertility Menstrual Irregularities Menopause-related Symptoms Neurological Conditions Parkinson’s Disease Alzheimer’s Disease Multiple Sclerosis Skin Disorders Psoriasis Eczema Metabolic & Endocrine Disorders Diabetes Obesity Thyroid Imbalances (Hypothyroidism, Hyperthyroidism) Mental & Emotional Well-being Stress Management Anxiety Depression ENT Disorders Tinnitus Meniere’s Disease Panchakarma Therapy & Ayurvedic Therapies We specialize in Kareli Panchakarma and other classical Ayurvedic therapies for detoxification and rejuvenation: Panchakarma Detox Treatments Ayurvedic Body Therapies Abhyanga (Ayurvedic Massage) Shirodhara (Oil Therapy for Mental Calmness) Treatments are tailored according to each individual’s constitution and health needs, ensuring safe, effective, and holistic healing. Book Your Consultation Experience authentic Ayurveda with one of Australia’s leading practitioners. 📞 Call us to book an appointment: 03 9794 8546 📍 Location: Ayurveda Yoga Wellness Clinic, Melbourne Our Ayurveda Professionals & Therapists At Ayurveda Yoga Wellness Clinic (AYWC), our dedicated team of experienced Panchakarma Therapists and Ayurvedic Practitioners works closely under the guidance of Dr. Santosh Kumar Yadav, our Chief Physician and Clinical Director. Together, they deliver authentic and personalized Ayurvedic therapies to support your health and healing journey. Our therapists are extensively trained in the classical Ayurvedic detoxification and rejuvenation therapies, with a focus on traditional Panchakarma procedures and specialized Ayurvedic bodywork. Specialization in Panchakarma & Rejuvenation Therapies Our team provides comprehensive Ayurvedic treatments including: Classical Panchakarma Procedures Vamana Karma – Emesis Therapy (Therapeutic vomiting for Kapha disorders) Virechana Karma – Purgation Therapy (Cleansing for Pitta imbalance) Anuvasana Vasti – Medicated Oil Enema Therapy Nirooha Vasti – Decoction Enema Therapy Nasya Karma – Nasal Administration of Medicated Oils Supportive Ayurvedic Therapies These procedures enhance the effectiveness of Panchakarma and are tailored based on individual needs: Snehana – Oleation Therapy (Internal and External) Swedana – Herbal Steam Therapy (Sudation) Therapeutic Ayurvedic Body Treatments Our clinic offers a wide range of Ayurvedic therapies designed for relaxation, detoxification, and deep tissue rejuvenation: Abhyanga – Full Body Ayurvedic Oil Massage Swedana – Herbal Steam Therapy Udvartana – Herbal Powder Massage for Lymphatic Stimulation & Weight Management Akshi Tarpana – Medicated Ghee/Oil Treatment for Eye Nourishment Elakizhi – Bolus Massage with Herbal Leaves Podikizhi – Bolus Massage with Herbal Powders Navarakizhi – Bolus Massage with Medicated Rice and Milk Head & Localized Ayurvedic Treatments Shirodhara – Continuous Stream of Oil on the Forehead (Mental Clarity & Calmness) Takra Dhara – Buttermilk Pouring Therapy (For Scalp & Mind Disorders) Ksheera Dhara – Medicated Milk Therapy for the Head Kati Vasti – Localized Oil Pool Treatment for Lower Back Pain Greeva Vasti – Localized Treatment for Neck & Cervical Spine Disorders Janu Vasti – Localized Therapy for Knee Joint Conditions Shiro Abhyanga – Traditional Indian Head Massage Ayurvedic Facial Massage – Natural Skin Rejuvenation and Relaxation All therapies are conducted with the utmost care and professionalism, using authentic herbal oils and medicines prepared according to traditional Ayurvedic formulations. Let our team support your journey to balance, vitality, and holistic well-being through time-honored Ayurvedic healing. Book Your Consultation with Dr Santosh ( Ayurveda Doctor). Experience authentic Ayurveda with one of Australia’s leading practitioners. 📞 Call us to book an appointment: 03 9794 8546 📍 Location: Ayurveda Yoga Wellness Clinic, Melbourne",
